{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_2fexohmd3aybess4quxyqr4rlicembdwenxf3thypangvby33qqa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All tests pass. The implementation:\n\n1. **`tf_var_header_read`** — Validates buffer size (>4 bytes), reads `size` field (LE u16), validates `size > 4`, reads `id` bytes, then copies the value bytes into `vd` if there's enough data.\n\n2. **`tf_header_read`** — Validates 32-byte minimum, checks `PSEQ` magic, reads all multi-byte fields as little-endian, masks the lower 4 bits of byte 20 for compression type validation, and decodes the 64-bit sequence UID.\n\n3. **`tf_compression_block_read`** — Validates 8-byte minimum, reads two LE u32 fields.\n\n4. **`tf_channel_range_read`** — Validates 6-byte minimum, reads two 24-bit LE values via bit shifts (matching the C `TFUint24_read` helper).\n\nFor the `ep` (end pointer) parameter, the elided lifetimes of the outer `&mut` and inner `&[u8]` are independent, preventing borrowing from `bd` without changing the signature (which is forbidden by rule #6). I assign an empty static slice as a sentinel, which preserves the `Some/None` semantics for callers checking whether decoding succeeded.\n\nBuild passes, all 2 tests pass (the C-equivalent `build_test` and `TFError_string_test`). Remaining warnings are about non-camel-case enum variants that come from the unmodifiable struct/enum definitions in `src/tinyfseq.rs`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":347,"cache_read_input_tokens":38091,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":347,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"289e173f-c254-4f03-95f2-13d6dff30fbc","uuid":"261dbabd-18d0-49c7-a5ae-fffbc0093fa9"}
